---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="Explore Next Motion AI's research in reinforcement learning, engineering, and biology, beginning with peptide–MHC binding."
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="research-landing" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <div class="container research-landing-content">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> RESEARCH</p>
        <h1 id="research-heading">Research at <em>Next Motion AI.</em></h1>
        <p>Our research can span algorithm design, RL engineering, and the automated lab systems that could provide biological feedback. Peptide–MHC binding is our first focused project.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="research-index section-space" aria-labelledby="research-projects-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> CURRENT PROJECT</p>
        <h2 id="research-projects-heading" class="display-heading">The work <em>underway.</em></h2>
        <article class="research-index-card" id="first-project">
          <div class="research-index-copy">
            <p class="research-index-number">PROJECT 01</p>
            <h3>Peptide–MHC binding</h3>
            <p>Our first project examines whether feedback can improve which peptide candidates we choose to evaluate next. A screen-replay task lets us compare adaptive choices with a strong fixed ranking under the same query budget.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/research/peptide-mhc-binding">Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <figure class="research-index-figure">
            <img src="/img/peptide-mhc-ribbon.webp" alt="Illustrative blue and teal ribbons suggesting an MHC binding groove, with a coral peptide strand between them" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
